CAT = "bcreLicensing"; SEG = "LIC"
Q = [
("Which activity counts as a trading service under the Real Estate Services Act?",
 "Showing a home to a buyer", ["Collecting strata fees", "Managing a tenant's repairs", "Filing a strata council's minutes"],
 "Trading services include showing real estate, advising on price, negotiating and presenting offers. Collecting strata fees is a strata management service and tenant repairs are rental property management."),
("A person helps an owner list and sell a house for a fee and holds no licence. Which statement is correct?",
 "That person is breaking the Act", ["Allowed if the owner agrees to it", "Allowed if no deposit is ever held", "Allowed for one sale each year"],
 "Section 3 bars anyone from providing real estate services to another for remuneration unless licensed or exempt. The owner's consent does not change that."),
("Which person is exempt from needing a real estate licence for services given in that role?",
 "A practising lawyer in their practice", ["A friend of the seller who helps out", "A mortgage lender's loan officer at work", "A neighbour of the seller's family home"],
 "The Act exempts people such as court-authorized persons, executors of an estate and practising lawyers acting in the course of their practice."),
("A representative licence authorizes the holder to provide services:",
 "Under a managing broker's supervision", ["As an independent business owner", "Through whichever brokerage they pick", "With no supervision from anyone"],
 "A representative works under the supervision of a managing broker of the one brokerage they are licensed with."),
("A representative is licensed with Brokerage A. May they also earn commission from Brokerage B?",
 "No, only through Brokerage A", ["Yes, if both agree", "Yes, on rental deals only", "Yes, if under half their income"],
 "A licensee must be licensed in relation to a single brokerage and must not accept remuneration for real estate services from anyone else."),
("What is the term of a standard real estate licence in British Columbia?",
 "2 years", ["1 year", "3 years", "5 years"],
 "Under the Rules, a licence term is 2 years, ending the day before the second anniversary of its effective date."),
("By when must a licensee apply to renew a licence that is ending?",
 "No later than 30 days before it ends", ["On the last day of the licence term", "Within 30 days after the term has ended", "At least one year before the term ends"],
 "The Rules require the renewal application no later than 30 days before the end of the current term."),
("What is the minimum age to be licensed as a real estate representative in BC?",
 "19", ["18", "21", "25"],
 "The Real Estate Services Act requires an applicant for licensing to be at least 19 years old and of good reputation."),
("Is arranging a lease of a home for a landlord, for a fee, a trading service under the Real Estate Services Act?",
 "Yes, a lease is a trade in real estate", ["No, only sales count as trades", "No, only leases over three years count", "Yes, but only for commercial space"],
 "Under the Act, trading in real estate includes leases, so arranging one for a landlord for remuneration requires a licence unless an exemption applies."),
("A representative's licence term ends and the renewal was never completed. May the person keep providing trading services?",
 "No, not until licensed again", ["Yes, for 30 days after it ends", "Yes, while the brokerage still employs them", "Yes, for existing clients only"],
 "Section 3 bars providing real estate services for remuneration without a licence, so services must stop when the licence ends until the person is licensed again."),
("A new trading services applicant has not yet finished the applied practice course. What can the superintendent issue?",
 "A temporary licence with a condition", ["A full licence with no conditions at all", "No licence of any kind until later on", "A brokerage licence in its place"],
 "A temporary licence conditional on completing the applied practice course, or having it waived, within the period set in the licence, may be issued."),
("Which act is professional misconduct for a licensee?",
 "Wrongful taking of client money", ["Declining a request for a showing", "Charging a higher listing price", "Working part-time hours as a licensee"],
 "Professional misconduct includes wrongful taking or deceptive dealing, contravening the Act or rules, incompetence and refusing to cooperate with an investigation."),
("Conduct unbecoming a licensee is conduct that, in the superintendent's judgment:",
 "Undermines public confidence", ["Costs the brokerage a client", "Breaks a personal contract", "Ends a service agreement early"],
 "The Act defines it as conduct contrary to the public interest, undermining public confidence or bringing the industry into disrepute."),
("A member of the public wants to file a complaint about a licensee. The complaint must be:",
 "In writing with particulars", ["Made by telephone only", "Sent in by the brokerage itself", "Verified by a lawyer first"],
 "A complaint to the superintendent must be in writing and include particulars. The superintendent acknowledges it unless it is anonymous."),
("A licensee learns that another regulator has started discipline proceedings against them. They must:",
 "Promptly notify the superintendent", ["Wait for a final decision on the case", "Tell only their own managing broker", "Tell the client on the next deal"],
 "A licensee must promptly give written notice of disciplinary or regulatory proceedings in BC or another jurisdiction that could lead to a sanction."),
("An unlicensed person did real estate work and sues for the commission. The court action:",
 "Cannot succeed under the Act", ["Succeeds if work was good", "Succeeds for half the fee", "Succeeds if the client agreed"],
 "No action may be brought for remuneration unless the claimant was licensed or exempt when the services were provided."),
("A licensee wants to pay a finder's fee to an unlicensed friend who found a buyer. This is:",
 "Prohibited by the Rules", ["Fine if it is under a limit", "Fine if the managing broker signs off", "Fine if paid in cash"],
 "A licensee must not pay or agree to pay remuneration to a person who is required to be licensed for those services but is not."),
("Besides the brokerage's name, what must a representative clearly show while providing services?",
 "Their own licensee name", ["Their licence expiry date", "Their managing broker's name", "Their home address"],
 "A licensee must clearly indicate their own licensee name, and a representative must also indicate the licensee name of the related brokerage."),
("Every brokerage must have at least one:",
 "Managing broker", ["Strata manager on staff", "Property appraiser on staff", "Mortgage broker on staff"],
 "A brokerage must have one or more managing brokers, who act for the brokerage and supervise its representatives and associate brokers."),
("Which duty belongs to the managing broker?",
 "Supervising related licensees", ["Setting each client's list price", "Writing every offer personally", "Choosing a buyer's lender"],
 "A managing broker must be actively engaged in management, ensure the business follows the Act and rules, and provide adequate supervision."),
("A representative learns of possible misconduct by a colleague. The representative must:",
 "Promptly notify the managing broker", ["Confront the colleague alone first", "Wait until the brokerage's next audit", "Report it to the superintendent only"],
 "A representative must promptly notify the managing broker on learning of conduct that may be professional misconduct or conduct unbecoming."),
("A licence category of 'trading services' alone permits the holder to:",
 "Act only on sales and leases", ["Also manage strata corporations", "Also manage rental buildings", "Also hold strata trust money"],
 "Categories are by service: a trading services licence does not cover rental property management or strata management, which need supplemental qualifications."),
("A superintendent asks a licensee a question about their business. The licensee must:",
 "Reply promptly", ["Reply within 90 days", "Reply only if a complaint exists", "Reply only through a lawyer"],
 "A licensee must reply promptly to the superintendent, and failing to cooperate with an investigation is itself professional misconduct."),
("A representative moves to a different brokerage. The representative:",
 "Must be licensed with the new brokerage", ["May keep serving old clients as before", "Needs only the old managing broker's consent", "May work for both brokerages at once"],
 "A licensee must be licensed in relation to, and engaged by, a single brokerage, so a move needs the licence amended to the new brokerage."),
]
